
######## Monday, the 5th of September, 1938 (mild (7° to 17°C)) ########
   ✦ The run begins in 1938: everybody is 7 years older than in January 1931.
   ✦ The papers of the years before: 25 days remembered.
   ✦ Mr. Thomas retires; Mr. Hale is chief clerk.
   ⚑ Arthur: In the summer of 1934 Joan, at eleven, won a place at the central school; she would stay at school till she is fifteen, and learn shorthand and book-keeping, while a girl who leaves at fourteen brings home ten shillings a week. Did Arthur let Joan take it? → YES (3:0) He lets her take it, because he thinks she may sometime earn a living by it.
   ✎ Joan is offered a central-school place; Arthur lets her take it.
   ✎ Joan left school in July 1938: a junior clerk in an office in the City, 12s. 6d. a week.
   ♥ Bert began walking out in August 1937 with Mary Jones, who works at Peek Frean's biscuit factory.
   ♥ Bert and Mary Jones were married on Saturday, the 30th of April, 1938.
   ⚑ Ada: Bert and Mary Jones were to be married on Saturday, the 30th of April, 1938, and they had no rooms of their own. Rooms in the Buildings are seven or eight shillings a week. Does Ada have them to live with her in her two rooms after the wedding, till they can find rooms of their own? → YES (3:0) She has them to live with her, because she likes the thought of Bert and Mary being married, and thinks it best for them to begin life independently.
   ♥ Bert and Mary Jones are married; they live with Ada.
   ◆ Ada's past: "He has been known to give a sixpence to a beggar in the street."
   ◆ Arthur's past: He had been told that, if he persevered in economy, he might look forward to a competency, and he did persevere.
   ◆ Mr. Thomas's past: He was never known to spend a shilling foolishly.
   📅 Ada means to: Tuesday: washes up, and cleans out the rooms
   📅 Arthur means to: Tuesday: calls on his mother, in Brixton, and takes her a florin | Wednesday: pays his rent, and on Thursday buy a pair of boots for Joan
   📅 Mr. Thomas means to: Tuesday: looks over his books and balance them for the half year | Wednesday: pays the household bills | Thursday: goes to the bank and receive the interest on his little capital
